<%# == One spec file, opened
        The rung BELOW the panel above, and the first surface here that narrows to a file rather
        than grouping by one. Every ranking on this page is a capped ten — ten examples, ten files,
        ten directories, ten moved areas — so a reader on a 20,000-example suite could learn that
        `spec/models/order_spec.rb` cost six minutes across three hundred examples and had no way
        whatever to learn WHICH three hundred. This panel is that way, and it opens off the row
        that stated the total.

        Rendered only when a file was ASKED for, and the read is taken only then: a page nobody
        asked a file of costs exactly what it cost before this existed.

        An EQUALITY predicate on `(test_run_id, spec_file_path)`, which is the composite index the
        by-file rollup's own plan certification says exists for this read and nothing else. A
        SUBTREE — "every example under `spec/models/`" — is a prefix predicate, wants a
        `text_pattern_ops` index and therefore a migration, and is deliberately not this panel.

        The list carries the file's UNTIMED examples, where every ranking above excludes theirs.
        They are the file's population: a reader looking at one file is owed its rows, and a list
        that dropped them would disagree with the count printed above it. That is why the ordering
        is `NULLS LAST` — see `SpecObservation.in_file`, where plain `DESC` would head a list
        captioned "slowest first" with the examples that never ran.

        Same visibility rule and same gate as the panels above: read-only suite telemetry on
        `current_repository(:view)`, outside `manage_keys`, and nothing here widens that. %>
<% if @spec_file_examples %>
      <%= render UI::PanelComponent.new(title: "Examples in this spec file", id: "spec-file-examples", class: "rc-drill") do |panel| %>
        <% panel.with_actions do %>
          <%# The way back OUT of THIS ask only: `spec_file: nil` is explicit because under carry-by-default an
              omission would mean "keep the file open". Every other ask — an open area, an open description,
              the branch, the window, the layer — rides through, so closing a file is not a request to
              close the area it was opened from. The anchor follows the area for the same reason. %>
          <%= render UI::ButtonComponent.new(
                variant: :ghost, size: :sm,
                href: drill_down_path(@repository, spec_file: nil,
                                      anchor: @spec_directory_request ? "spec-directory-files" : "spec-file-durations")
              ) { "Close file" } %>
        <% end %>
        <% if @spec_file_examples.recorded? %>
          <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "spec-file-examples-basis") do %>
            <span class="font-mono text-app-content-secondary"><%= @spec_file_examples.path %></span>
            — <%= spec_file_examples_scope_sentence(@spec_file_examples) %>
            <% if @spec_file_examples.complete? %>
              <% if @spec_file_examples.truncated? %>
                Every one of the
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_examples.recorded_count) %> reported a
                duration, so the ranking these
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_examples.rows.size) %> were drawn from covers
                the whole of what this run recorded here — the cap is all that keeps the rest off
                this page.
              <% else %>
                Every one of them reported a duration, so the list covers the whole of what this
                run recorded here.
              <% end %>
            <% elsif @spec_file_examples.any_timed? %>
              Durations here cover <%= @spec_file_examples.coverage_label %> — the same fraction
              the row for this file states in the panel above.
              <% if @spec_file_examples.untimed_omitted_count.zero? %>
                The other <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_examples.untimed_count) %> reported
                none and sit at the END of the list rather than at the head of it.
              <% elsif @spec_file_examples.lists_untimed? %>
                The other <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_examples.untimed_count) %> reported
                none:
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_examples.shown_untimed_count) %> of those are
                at the END of this list rather than at the head of it, and the remaining
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_examples.untimed_omitted_count) %> are not on
                this page at all.
              <% else %>
                The other <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_examples.untimed_count) %> reported
                none, and the cap was reached before the list got to any of them — none are on
                this page at all.
              <% end %>
              An example that never ran has no duration to report, so a missing timing is a
              faithful record rather than a gap — and it is not a zero.
            <% end %>
            Each row names where it is DEFINED, which for an example coming from a shared example
            group is a different file from this one — this list is what this file RAN.
            Counted off the rows this run wrote here, which is a different figure from the suite
            size on the Summary at the top of this page and may legitimately differ from it.
          <% end %>
          <%= render UI::TableComponent.new(
                columns: ["Test", "Layer", { label: "Duration", end: true }, "Outcome"],
                describedby: "spec-file-examples-basis", sortable: true) do %>
            <% @spec_file_examples.rows.each do |observation| %>
              <%= drawer_row(observation.id, kind: "Test", title: observation.label,
                    facts: [["Defined at", observation.location_label], ["Declared layer", observation.intent_layer.presence || "undeclared"],
                            ["Declared entity", observation.intent_entity], ["Declared action", observation.intent_action],
                            ["Declared behavior", observation.intent_behavior], ["Duration", observation.duration_label],
                            ["Outcome", observation.outcome_label]],
                    actions: [*(observation.name.present? ? [["Run by run", drill_down_path(@repository, unstable_test: observation.name, unstable_test_from: "slowest-examples", anchor: "unstable"), :primary]] : []),
                              ["Open on GitHub", @repository.github_blob_url(observation.file_path, observation.line_number, @latest_test_run.commit_sha), :ghost]]) do %>
                <td>
                  <%= row_open(observation.label) %>
                  <span class="rc-sec mono"><%= observation.location_label %></span>
                  <%= render "repositories/authored_intent", observation: observation %>
                </td>
                <td><%= declared_layer_label(observation) %></td>
                <td class="num" data-sort="<%= observation.duration_seconds %>"><%= observation.duration_label %></td>
                <td><%= render UI::BadgeComponent.new(tone: observation.outcome_tone) { observation.outcome_label } %></td>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No examples for this file",
                description: "This run recorded no examples in #{@spec_file_examples.path}. It " \
                             "may have been renamed or deleted since, or never have run in this " \
                             "run at all — the “Heaviest spec files” table lists the files " \
                             "this run did record."
              ) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
